Article 27 In any of the following circumstances, a resolution of the shareholders' meeting or the board of directors of a company shall not be established:
(1) A resolution was made without convening a meeting of the shareholders' meeting or the board of directors;
(2) The shareholders' meeting or the board of directors meeting did not vote on the matter of the resolution;
(3) The number of persons present at the meeting or the number of voting rights held did not meet the requirements of this Law or the company's articles of association;
(4) The number of persons who voted in favor of the resolution or the number of voting rights held did not meet the requirements of this Law or the company's articles of association.

Article 32 The registration items of a company include:
(1) Name;
(2) Domicile;
(3) Registered capital;
(4) Business scope;
(5) Name of the legal representative;
(6) Names or titles of the shareholders of a limited liability company and the promoters of a joint stock limited company.
The company registration authority shall publicly disclose the aforesaid registration items of the company through the National Enterprise Credit Information Publicity System.

Article 40 A company shall, in accordance with regulations, publicly disclose the following items through the National Enterprise Credit Information Publicity System:
(1) The amount, method, and date of capital contributions subscribed and paid by shareholders of a limited liability company, and the number of shares subscribed by promoters of a joint stock limited company;
(2) Information on changes in equity or shares of shareholders of a limited liability company and promoters of a joint stock limited company;
(3) Information on the acquisition, change, and cancellation of administrative licenses;
(4) Other information as provided by laws and administrative regulations.
A company shall ensure that the information disclosed in the preceding paragraph is authentic, accurate, and complete.

Article 178 A person shall not serve as a director, supervisor, or senior officer of a company under any of the following circumstances:
(1) having no capacity for civil conduct or having limited capacity for civil conduct;
(2) having been sentenced to criminal punishment for embezzlement, bribery, misappropriation of property, or sabotage of the socialist market economic order, or having been deprived of political rights due to a crime, and less than five years have elapsed since the completion of the execution of the punishment; or, if a suspended sentence is imposed, less than two years have elapsed since the expiration of the probation period;
(3) having served as a director, factory director, or manager of a company or enterprise that went bankrupt due to liquidation, and bearing personal responsibility for the bankruptcy of such company or enterprise, and less than three years have elapsed since the completion of the bankruptcy liquidation of such company or enterprise;
(4) having served as the legal representative of a company or enterprise whose business license was revoked or which was ordered to close for illegal activities, and bearing personal responsibility therefor, and less than three years have elapsed since the date of such revocation or closure;
(5) being listed by a People's Court as a dishonest person subject to enforcement due to failure to pay off a relatively large amount of due debt.
Where a director, supervisor, or senior officer is elected, appointed, or engaged in violation of the preceding paragraph, such election, appointment, or engagement shall be invalid.
If a director, supervisor, or senior officer falls under any of the circumstances set forth in the first paragraph during their tenure of office, the company shall remove them from their position.

Article 181 Directors, supervisors, and senior officers shall not engage in any of the following acts:
(1) misappropriating company property or embezzling company funds;
(2) depositing company funds in accounts opened in their own name or in the name of other individuals;
(3) using their positions to solicit bribes or accept other illegal income;
(4) accepting commissions from third parties in transactions with the company and keeping them for themselves;
(5) disclosing company secrets without authorization;
(6) other acts in violation of the duty of loyalty to the company.

Article 183 Directors, supervisors, and senior officers shall not use their positions to seek business opportunities belonging to the company for themselves or others, except under any of the following circumstances:
(1) reporting to the board of directors or the shareholders' meeting and obtaining a resolution approved by the board of directors or the shareholders' meeting in accordance with the provisions of the articles of association;
(2) where the company cannot take advantage of such business opportunity in accordance with the provisions of laws, administrative regulations, or the articles of association.

Article 195 For public issuance of company bonds, the company shall register with the securities regulatory authority of the State Council and announce the method for raising company bonds.
The method for raising company bonds shall specify the following main matters:
(1) the name of the company;
(2) the use of the funds raised from the bonds;
(3) the total amount of the bonds and their face value;
(4) the method for determining the bond interest rate;
(5) the term and method for repayment of principal and payment of interest;
(6) the bond guarantee situation;
(7) the issuing price of the bonds and the start and end dates of issuance;
(8) the net asset value of the company;
(9) the total amount of company bonds already issued but not yet due;
(10) the underwriting institution for the company bonds.

Article 198 Where a company issues company bonds, it shall maintain a register of company bondholders.
For issuance of company bonds, the register of company bondholders shall specify the following matters:
(1) the name or title and domicile of each bondholder;
(2) the date on which the bondholder acquired the bonds and the bond numbers;
(3) the total amount of the bonds, the face value, interest rate, term and method for repayment of principal and payment of interest;
(4) the date of issuance of the bonds.

Article 229 A company shall be dissolved under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The term of operation stipulated in the company's articles of association expires, or any other ground for dissolution stipulated in the articles of association occurs;
(2) A resolution on dissolution is adopted by the shareholders' meeting;
(3) Dissolution is necessary due to the merger or division of the company;
(4) The business license is revoked according to law, or the company is ordered to close down or is revoked;
(5) The People's Court orders the dissolution of the company in accordance with Article 231 of this Law.
Where any ground for dissolution specified in the preceding paragraph occurs, the company shall, within ten days, publish the ground for dissolution on the national enterprise credit information publicity system.

Article 234 During the liquidation period, the liquidation group shall exercise the following powers:
(1) To sort out the company's property and prepare a balance sheet and a detailed list of assets respectively;
(2) To notify creditors and make public announcements;
(3) To handle unfinished business of the company related to the liquidation;
(4) To pay off the taxes owed and the taxes incurred during the liquidation process;
(5) To clear claims and debts;
(6) To distribute the remaining property of the company after the settlement of debts;
(7) To represent the company in participating in civil action activities.

Article 254 Any of the following acts shall be punished by the finance department of the people's government at or above the county level in accordance with the "Accounting Law of the People's Republic of China" and other laws and administrative regulations:
(1) Setting up separate accounting books outside the statutory accounting books;
(2) Providing financial and accounting reports containing false records or concealing material facts.
